{meta title='Sums, integrals and limits', about='The limits of a sum go under and over it, those of an integral beside it; inline they move aside to keep the line low.'/}
{math display='block'}sum_(i=1)^n i^2 = (n(n+1)(2n+1))/6{/math}
{math display='block'}int_0^1 x^2 dx = 1/3, quad lim_(x->oo) (1 + 1/x)^x = e{/math}
<p>Inline: {math 'sum_(k=0)^oo 1/(k!) = e'/} and {math}f'(x) = lim_(h->0) (f(x+h) - f(x))/h{/math}.</p>
